From: Angelpro09xd <167892325+Angelpro09xd@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sapphire-0249: Goodix probe: libgf_hal's wakeup sequence (milestone 1b)

0248's PRE_DETECT reached the TA and came back GF_ERROR_SPI_TRANSFER_ERROR
(1025): libgf_hal wakes the sensor first. Op 1 now restarts goodixfp cleanly
(APP_SHUTDOWN if loaded, APP_START), powers the sensor (L9, gpio65, 10 ms,
reset pulse low 5 ms / high / 60 ms), sends WAKEUP (1002,9) with
reset-before-wakeup (+0x1d 0xff, +0x1e 1), a hardware reset pulse when it
answers 0, WAKEUP again (+0x1e 0), then PRE_DETECT and DETECT_SENSOR, retried
after a reset pulse only on FAILED_AND_RETRY (0x458). gf error codes are logged
by name; envelope +0x1c mirrors the gf result and is no longer a transport
failure; the whitelist table is 64 bytes. Op 4 restarts the TA only, op 5 runs
op 1 reusing a loaded TA. Read-only logs of gpio14..17, gpio104, gpio83 and
the GCC QUPv3 wrapper 0 / SE5 clock branches around the wakeup.
fp_diag reads only gpio104/83: the SE5 SPI pins and QUP clocks belong to TZ.
---
 bsd/dev/sweet_qsee_ctl.c       |   7 +-
 iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetQsee.cpp | 327 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----------
 2 files changed, 250 insertions(+), 84 deletions(-)

